<H1 align="center">Constructing Gröbner Basis by Interpolation</H1>

<h3 align="center">
<A HREF="../../participants.html#Sauer">Thomas Sauer</A><br>
</h3>

Date: July 18th (Thursday) <br>
Time: 11:35-12:00 <br>

<center>
Abstract
</center>

 The talk is concerned with an algorithm to find a minimal Groebner basis for an
    ideal which is given as the joint kernel of linearly independent linear functionals - the
    generic example is Lagrange interpolation at a finite set of pairwise distinct points. The
    method results from constructing a particular polynomial subspace which admits unqiue
    interpolation and satisfies certain other constraints. 

